{
 "_source": [
  "Mainnet, read 2026-11-20 from public nodes (getSignaturesForAddress, reads only): the buyers of three pump.fun coins in the trades ryntra.io showed, and how long each wallet's history really is.",
  "`quietButOld`: the largest buyer ($171) of a coin three minutes old. A node that keeps a day and a half of history lists twelve signatures for it, the oldest sixteen hours back — it looks new. Its whole history, from a node that keeps everything, is the list here: 139 signatures since July 2025.",
  "`verified`: the buyers a short-history node listed with few signatures (under a hundred for the first coin, under forty for the second), read again whole. `signatures` is the whole count (`more`: a thousand and more), `firstHoursAgo` the first signature's age at the read (with `more`, the thousandth newest's).",
  "Of 93 buyers of the first coin (an hour old) none has under 100 signatures: the twenty a short-history node listed with under a hundred were read whole, the least has 244. Of 123 buyers of the second (seven minutes old) thirteen of the twenty-two candidates were read whole: none is under 20 signatures, three are under 40 and younger than 72 hours.",
  "Of 77 buyers of the third (three minutes old: its whole life is in the trades) fifty have under forty signatures in the last day and a half, the largest among them. Six of the eight largest — the eight the engine read first — were read whole: 68 to 213 signatures each, the first of them fourteen to sixteen months back. An old farm of wallets, not fresh ones."
 ],
